# --- Licence-restricted corpora. Never commit these. ---
# MSMT17 is 2.7 GB of redistribution-restricted person crops. The ReID operating point is
# already fitted and the result is committed (results/reid_eval.md), so the corpus buys
# nothing here and publishing it would breach its terms.
MSMT17/
Market-1501*/
Charades*/
Le2i*/
CAUCAFall*/
URFD*/

# Toyota Smarthome. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC (github.com/PARTHG0106/BehaviorSense), and the
# dataset is licensed for academic research only, granted per-request to one institutional
# address. That makes every part of it unpublishable here - and not only the video:
#
#   Toyota_Smarthome/*.pdf     Inria's licence text, theirs not ours to relicense
#   Toyota_Smarthome/*.txt     the dataset's own READMEs
#   smarthome_C[SV]_51.json    the aggregated annotations. Publicly mirrored by the authors
#                              on GitHub, which is THEIR choice to make and not ours to
#                              repeat from a repo carrying an MIT licence file.
#   Annotation/                the per-video CSVs from Annotation_v1.0.tar.gz
#
# The annotation JSON is needed OFFLINE for the duration cross-check, so it is staged the
# way every other restricted asset here is: fetched by an online notebook into a PRIVATE
# Kaggle dataset. `src/behaviorsense/data/toyota.py` carries only class names, protocol
# subject ids and the mapping - facts about the corpus, not the corpus.
Toyota_Smarthome/
toyota_smarthome*/
smarthome_CS_51.json
smarthome_CV_51.json
TSU_CS.json
Annotation/
Annotation_v1.0*/

# --- Model weights: third-party redistribution + git bloat ---
# weights/osnet_ain_x1_0_{imagenet,msmt17}.pth are upstream checkpoints, not ours to
# relicense. scripts/ documents where to fetch them.
weights/
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine
*.safetensors

# --- Derived data and session output ---
# data/shards/_smoke*.npz are synthetic fixtures, regenerable on CPU in seconds - and one
# of them once contaminated a real fall corpus when it rode along in an upload.
data/
datasets/
runs/
results/embeddings/
*.npz
*.npy
*.db

# --- Media ---
media/
*.mp4
*.avi

# --- Local config ---
configs/local.yaml
configs/*.local.yaml

# --- Frontend ---
node_modules/
dashboard/dist/

# --- Credentials ---
# A Kaggle API token is a username plus a key that can create, overwrite and delete every
# dataset on the account. `kaggle (1).json` sits at this repo root, untracked but NOT ignored,
# and `origin` is a public GitHub repository - one `git add .` publishes the key. It lives at
# ~/.kaggle/kaggle.json for the CLI to read; the copy here is a download artefact and does not
# need to exist at all.
kaggle*.json
*.kaggle.json
# biometric templates - the operator's enrolled residents; must never be committed
gallery.json
